# Phase-4 replay archive — the spawn-report-in-flight race: the pickup wins
# the race against its own spawn report (the pickup lands while the spawn
# report is still delayed on the wire). The host's pending-pickup queue holds
# the claim for up to 500 ms; when the spawn lands inside the hold the SAME
# transfer the spawn-first path would have produced settles — no reject, no
# local rollback. The spawn relay is source-excluded and the settled pickup
# relay reaches the other guest exactly once (the carried-fact sync rides the
# same settlement), so G1 sees no wire echo and G2 sees pickup without spawn.
#
# Fossil of: ItemRaceTests.SpawnPickupInflight_PickupArrivesFirst_SettlesWhenTheSpawnLands
# Mechanism: ItemService.PendingPickups.cs — PendingPickupQueue hold + spawn settlement

@0 pickup g1 42 test_item 1.0
@0 fault g1 host delay=300
@0 spawn g1 42 test_item 1.0
@33 expect_no_reject g1
@333 expect no_host_table 42 within 500
@333 expect_no_reject g1
